      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_and_function -> function_only (paper reports surface: not_reported, function: yes). Paper (PMID 40140957): \"The HA epitope (YPYDVPDYA) was inserted by conventional PCR after glycine 212, corresponding to the S5 end\". Audit note: Kv4.3 cDNA from J.M. Nerbonne, species not stated; rat and human Kv4.3 are identical over 202-222 (offset 0), so G212 holds either way. 'S5 end' is the paper's label; 212 is in the S1-S2 loop. Only anti-HA Western blots, no surface staining; biophysical properties unchanged vs WT (not shown).] L4 names G212 as the insertion point in full-length Kv4.3. Python lookup confirms residue 212 = G and 213 = S, both within extracellular span 204-227, 9 aa from TM1 end (203) and 16 aa from TM2 start (228), satisfying the \u22653 aa TM-distance constraint. The paper's 'S5 end' label is a paper-internal naming convention; the canonical topology places this residue in the S1-S2 loop. L5 confirms preserved biophysical properties. Ranked second because surface detection by immunofluorescence is not explicitly reported for this construct. Full-length Kv4.3 (KCND3); HA tag inserted by conventional PCR after G212, described as 'corresponding to the S5 end' in the source paper (PMC11938557). Position 212 falls within the S1-S2 extracellular loop (topology span 204-227). The paper's 'S5' label likely reflects an internal segment-numbering convention distinct from canonical S1-S6 TM nomenclature; the position is unambiguously extracellular by the authoritative topology. Correct in-frame insertion confirmed by DNA sequencing.",
